Fix the HAVE_UDATA_TO_DRV_CONTEXT conftest under clang on Linux 6.18.

The conftest invokes rdma_udata_to_drv_context() as a bare statement and
discards its value. Since Linux 6.18 the macro casts its null branch:

    (udata ? container_of(...) : (drv_dev_struct *)NULL)

which makes clang report -Wunused-value. The kernel build promotes that to an
error, so the conftest fails to compile and HAVE_UDATA_TO_DRV_CONTEXT is left
undefined even though the kernel provides the macro. gcc does not warn here,
so the failure only shows up on a clang-built kernel.

The driver then compiles its pre-5.1 fallbacks. In efa_create_user_cq() the
fallback is

    struct efa_ucontext *ucontext = to_ecq(ibcq)->ucontext;

which reads the field out of a CQ the RDMA core has just zero-allocated
(HAVE_CQ_CORE_ALLOCATION is defined), so ucontext is NULL. It is stored back
into cq->ucontext and dereferenced a few lines later:

    params.uarn = cq->ucontext->uarn;

That is a NULL pointer dereference at offset 0x70, inside the CQ_CREATE
ioctl, so every fi_cq_open() against the device panics the kernel.

Assign the result to a variable so the expression is used.

--- a/kernel/linux/efa/config/efa.cmake
+++ b/kernel/linux/efa/config/efa.cmake
@@ -171,7 +171,10 @@
   "
   "
 struct ib_udata *udata;
-rdma_udata_to_drv_context(udata, struct efa_ucontext, ibucontext);
+struct efa_ucontext *ucontext;
+
+ucontext = rdma_udata_to_drv_context(udata, struct efa_ucontext, ibucontext);
+(void)ucontext;
   "
   HAVE_UDATA_TO_DRV_CONTEXT "")
 
